FILE qualification_failure_revision02_architecture_codex/20261015-current-chat/STOP-ARCHITECTURE.md
# STOP revision02 — exact retained-handle controlled crash stop

DESIGN_ONLY; no actual process, signal, database connection, backup or termination has been performed. This source/fixture contract is independent of A/B/C. Any actual stop requires a later separately reviewed exact operation plan. Console-wide CTRL_C_EVENT is prohibited for the already running Core: member enumeration does not create atomic exclusivity. That branch returns STOP_UNAVAILABLE and is not implemented as a fallback.

## Scope and source dependency

Create a standalone `ops/owned_core_stop` command. The native handle capability belongs to a new supervisor file; authority/proof/plan orchestration belongs to `internal/ownedcorestop`, which may import host/domain/runtime/store. Supervisor must not import domain/host (domain already imports supervisor). No edits to control main, normal shutdown, SDK, existing release ProcessDriver or Desktop are required. Keep actual-image observation limit separate from fixture launch policy. Exact files are in STOP-exact-scope.json.

This is an explicitly named crash stop. It does not report graceful shutdown, resolve the old Run, reconcile money, resume execution, create a next attempt or restart any process. A future exact Core with appropriate evidence may be targeted only once. Never terminate by process name/tree/PID alone, kill the Desktop, close arbitrary remote handles or terminate a job containing unapproved processes.

## Frozen plan and retained capability

`preflight --input <strict subject JSON> --operation-id <id> --out <new outside-data-root directory>` reads only public source/build/native/state metadata and creates a protected same-SID output directory. It does NOT signal/terminate or acquire a product mutation capability. It produces the canonical full stop plan plus SQLite online backup and logical census, input hashes and eligibility findings. An ineligible result cannot be upgraded by a command-line force flag. External F01 provenance must be provided and independently accepted, never manufactured by the helper.

`commit --plan <path> --expect-plan-sha256 <hash>` is a separate invocation requiring the reviewed plan. Open one non-inherited Core handle with QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION|SYNCHRONIZE|PROCESS_TERMINATE and retain it through all checks, one termination and native wait. Derive PID (GetProcessId), creation time (GetProcessTimes), process token SID and image path from THAT handle. Open/retain a no-reparse image file handle, verify bounded bytes/hash and stable file identity while held; no generic ObserveProcess observation is a stop capability. Compare canonical path/image digest/create time/SID/Host/data-root/known Desktop parent identity with the plan and accepted historical READY/build chain. Verify the exact Desktop parent with its own retained read/query handle. Parent identity comparison is observational; no parent termination authority exists. Reject malformed paths, reparse, foreign SID/Host/Owner-root, PID reuse, executable replacement or mismatch.

Open/query authority through a dedicated public same-SID Host/Owner reader. It must not initialize Host state, issue credentials or read private keys. Exact plan includes current unrevoked Owner id/root, Host public state/hash, schema24 fingerprint, database canonical file identity, operation namespace, allowed subject old Run/epoch/request/dispatch and original worker/verifier identities. Stop is not available merely because the caller can open PROCESS_TERMINATE.

## Historical fence proof for this specific old Core

The actual subject may have Run RUNNING and dispatch UNKNOWN; that is why maintenance is needed. Do not reject this exact permitted terminal-maintenance subject solely on those two states. UNKNOWN **external effect outcome** is forbidden; UNKNOWN money on a CONFIRMED MODEL remains unchanged and is not such an outcome.

Required conjunctive proof before issuing a stop capability:

1. Root F01 inputs bind the SAME live Core creation identity and image to reviewed Main4f code and startup `store.Open -> Ready`, with WAL/FULL verified by that startup. A newly opened helper connection's PRAGMA synchronous does not prove the live Core setting.
2. The exact consumed original request and qualification marker prove that this Core successfully passed `BeginLocalQualificationWindow` before startRuntimeVerifier and ExecuteLocalQualification. Main4f `runtime_qualification_confirmation_windows.go:235` is the only production assignment to qualificationActive=true; `:251` is its only clearing assignment. `EndLocalQualificationWindow` returns first at unresolved Run/dispatch/effect check `:249`, so the original unresolved subject prevents clearing. Core must not have restarted since that request. This is a code+historical-facts proof, not a private-memory read.
3. `Scan` first refuses qualificationActive, then independently refuses the durable `managedQualificationUnsettled` fence. Any subsequent CONFIRM calls Begin first and fails before verifier launch because the old window remains active. `DesktopManagement.Serve` is serial; no parallel management action creates another verifier. Map all production native launch/effect entry points to these gates; no unknown alternate bypass may remain. No new CONFIRM probe is used as evidence.
4. All old worker and original verifier native lifetimes have exact independent closure evidence (identity/creation, process wait or equivalent accepted OS closure, original worker job drained and owner.lock released). Absence of a PID from a current list is insufficient. Pending unknown native child or unrecorded launch rejects.
5. Every external effect in the complete current census is terminal CONFIRMED/known non-applied, with exact request/receipt hashes. The minimal actual v1 expects only the original confirmed MODEL chain and zero TOOL/SOURCE/EXPERIMENT. All other dispatches must be terminal and native closed; only the exact allowlisted old subject may retain UNKNOWN dispatch. No prepared/started/unknown external effect, additional native child, pending unmatched client/provider operation or different unresolved subject is allowed.

If any conjunct is unproved, return STOP_UNAVAILABLE with the missing proof; source/fixture success cannot replace actual historical proof. The observed verifier-before-Run-consumption order is safe for this old Core only because the retained original qualification window is proven and every new verifier launch must pass Begin first. Do not generalize this to arbitrary Core instances or newly started servers.

## STOP-only SQLite commit barrier: explicit limited exception

Root accepted this as a DESIGN exception; actual use is not yet authorized. A helper can take a short SQLite writer reservation while Core owns DataRootLease ONLY to prevent additional durable preparation between the census and termination. This does not confer product write authority. Open the existing database in `mode=rw` with no create, migrate, store.Open, journal-mode change or persistent PRAGMA. Use one dedicated connection, bounded busy wait and `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`; after successful acquisition set connection-local `PRAGMA query_only=ON`, read it back, and retain the reserved writer lock. Native fixture MUST demonstrate query_only preserves the acquired writer reservation and blocks DML/DDL. A private statement authorizer admits only exact fixed SELECT catalog, BEGIN IMMEDIATE, ROLLBACK and query_only toggling/check; no user-supplied SQL, ATTACH, VACUUM, writable_schema, extension load, transaction commit or persistent pragma. Raw connection never escapes this package. Defense in depth: underlying SQLite query_only must reject a deliberately injected direct INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL in tests. If this cannot be established with the pinned driver, STOP_UNAVAILABLE and revise source contract; do not remove this guard.

Take the final schema/Host/Owner/current request/Run/dispatch/client-request/effect census AFTER the barrier is acquired, in that same snapshot. A Core transaction that commits while the helper waits must appear and be evaluated. Reject any PREPARED/STARTED/UNKNOWN effect or unexplained extra subject. Prove provider/tool invocation occurs only after durable PREPARED commit, and worker launch only after durable matching dispatch state; existing prepared work is not neutralized by the lock and must be absent/closed before stop. The qualification-window proof above blocks the pre-consumption verifier path. Thus lock plus complete existing-work census plus gate proof, not the lock alone, establishes no newly admitted external work. Any discovered ungated action makes stop unavailable.

Keep the reservation until the exact Core handle reports exit, then ROLLBACK and close it. Do not COMMIT even an allegedly empty transaction. On any failure/deadline before termination, rollback/close without a signal. A lock timeout is not permission to terminate. No lease borrowing, row insertion, update or deletion occurs through this exception.

## Online backup and stable baseline

Use pinned modernc.org/sqlite v1.60.1 native online backup API via a separate source `sql.Conn.Raw` implementing `NewBackup(string) (*sqlite.Backup,error)`, bounded Step and Finish, to a create-new protected destination outside data root. API availability was checked in installed module conn.go/backup.go; this is not live backup proof. Do not use current general CreateBackup: it performs broader export/key/protected-store work. Do not copy hot db/WAL files or run checkpoint/VACUUM against Core. Backup destination can contain database-private content; only its hash/census are published, access stays current SID, no credential contents are printed.

Chosen v1 sequence avoids backing up through the reserved source connection: preflight performs online backup, closes+flushes destination, opens backup read-only, validates quick_check and canonical full logical census; plan binds that backup/hash/census. Commit then obtains the reservation and compares the full current logical database census with the frozen backup baseline. All tables, primary-key rows, BLOB hashes and sqlite_master schema are included; volatile connection-level values and physical WAL byte layout are excluded. Drift means STALE_PLAN and zero termination; do not silently take another backup or alter reviewed plan. A new preflight/review is required. A separate read connection under the barrier is optional future work, not needed in v1; never run backup from the reserved connection and assume it cannot deadlock.

## One action and postflight

Output journal is private outside product data in the reviewed operation directory. Use create-new canonical `plan.json`, `backup-manifest.json`, `BEGIN.json`, `TERMINATE_INTENT.json`, `NATIVE_EXIT.json`, `POSTFLIGHT.json`; flush before advancing. No file is overwritten. Under final barrier/retained-handle/proof checks, persist TERMINATE_INTENT, call TerminateProcess on the SAME Core handle once using a fixed explicit maintenance exit code, then WaitForSingleObject with bounded deadline and obtain numeric exit code from that same handle. If the Core has already exited, make no termination call and report observed-before-signal state separately. A timeout/failure after the single call is UNKNOWN, not a retry opportunity. No fallback signal or process restart is allowed.

After observed Core exit, release the SQLite reservation, then acquire the real DataRootLease. Verify quick_check, schema/authority and complete logical census equals the reviewed baseline, with zero new request/effect/ledger/Run mutations caused by the helper. Core's in-flight uncommitted DB transaction can roll back naturally; committed baseline must survive. Physical WAL checkpoint/removal is permitted. Any logical drift/integrity failure yields STOP_OBSERVED_MAINTENANCE_BLOCKED, retaining evidence; never restore backup automatically. Native exit proof and lease acquisition are required before STOPPED_LEASE_VERIFIED. Release lease only when helper finishes; subsequent C must reacquire and re-preflight, never inherit stop as terminal fact authority.

Recovery is observation-only. If helper dies after TERMINATE_INTENT, a later `inspect` may classify missing/partial proof and current exact identity but cannot issue a second termination or claim native wait evidence it never held. Ambiguity is UNKNOWN; any further stop requires a new separately reviewed operation. Crash before action means NOT_APPLIED only with complete unchanged identity/evidence; it is not automatically retried. Completed operation is immutable and re-read returns identical result.

## Required acceptance

STOP-test-cuts.json requires real Windows process handles and WAL tests, not mocked process lists or SQLite JSON. Include same-console unrelated child to prove no console API is called; PID-reuse/identity drift; lock wait transaction races; query_only/DML denial; existing PREPARED refusal; queued provider blocked behind commit; retained window verifier gate; backup drift; controlled crash with committed/inflight WAL; termination count exactly one; native wait/lease; and each journal crash point. Source+fixture acceptance grants no authority to stop the current Core. Actual plan requires accepted F01/worker/verifier proofs and explicit review of the STOP-only reservation exception.

